{"kind": "journal", "text": "Final selection logic: three robust effects found - short-horizon reversal (ma(3)/neg ret(5), strongest), short-lookback vol premium (std(10)-std(20)), and medium-lookback skewness (skew(120), positive at 40/60/120 lookbacks). Additive cs_z composites of these sit on a broad plateau (SR 1.1-1.35 across ~40 variants), so top-of-plateau picks should carry OOS. Reporting three plateau variants that differ mildly in vol lookback and skew weight to hedge tuning risk; avoided putting the 2x-skew weight in all picks since skew(250) is flat. Stopping at 6/12 batches to limit selection bias.", "ts": "2026-09-01T06:20:59.152043+00:00"}
{"kind": "report", "top3_chosen": ["add(add(add(cs_z(ma(3)), cs_z(neg(ret(5)))), cs_z(std(10))), add(cs_z(skew(120)), cs_z(skew(120))))", "add(add(cs_z(ma(3)), cs_z(std(10))), cs_z(skew(120)))", "add(add(add(cs_z(ma(3)), cs_z(neg(ret(5)))), cs_z(std(20))), cs_z(skew(120)))"], "chosen_sr_train": [1.3503, 1.3046, 1.2555], "rationale": "Panel is driven by three additive cross-sectional effects: short-horizon mean reversion (price below its 3-5d MA outperforms; ret(5) SR -0.90 standalone), a short-lookback volatility premium (std(10)-std(20) positive), and positive medium-lookback skewness (skew(120), positive across 40-120d lookbacks). Equal-weight cs_z composites of these legs form a broad stable plateau (train SR 1.1-1.35, IC ~0.006-0.007 across ~40 parameterizations), indicating the edge is structural rather than a tuning artifact. The three picks are plateau variants differing only in vol lookback (10 vs 20) and skew weight (1x vs 2x) to hedge parameter-selection risk.", "n_batches_used": 6, "ts": "2026-09-01T06:21:05.958729+00:00"}
